From: CoolFreeze23 <34906576+CoolFreeze23@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: do not leave a freed REO queue published on tid setup failure

When ath12k_dp_prepare_reo_update_elem() fails in
ath12k_dp_rx_peer_tid_setup(), the descriptor is freed through the copy
in rx_tid->qbuf, but the TID stays marked active and
dp_peer->reoq_bufs[tid] still points at the freed memory. The next
ADDBA for that TID takes the "already set up" branch and programs the
freed DMA address into REO (UPDATE_RX_QUEUE) and, on IPQ5332, into
firmware (WMI_PEER_REORDER_QUEUE_SETUP). The hardware then writes into
a recycled object for the rest of the association.

Clear the active bit, and free the buffer and its per-peer slot only if
this call allocated it. The same code is in mainline.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
@@ -607,6 +607,7 @@ int ath12k_dp_rx_peer_tid_setup(struct ath12k *ar, const u8 *peer_mac, int vdev_
 	struct ath12k_dp_link_peer *peer;
 	struct ath12k_dp_rx_tid *rx_tid;
 	dma_addr_t paddr_aligned;
+	bool new_qbuf;
 	int ret;
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&dp->dp_lock);
@@ -669,6 +670,7 @@ int ath12k_dp_rx_peer_tid_setup(struct ath12k *ar, const u8 *peer_mac, int vdev_
 
 	rx_tid->ba_win_sz = ba_win_sz;
 
+	new_qbuf = !peer->dp_peer->reoq_bufs[tid].vaddr;
 	ret = ath12k_dp_arch_rx_assign_reoq(dp, peer->dp_peer, rx_tid, ssn, pn_type);
 	if (ret) {
 		spin_unlock_bh(&dp->dp_lock);
@@ -686,7 +688,18 @@ int ath12k_dp_rx_peer_tid_setup(struct ath12k *ar, const u8 *peer_mac, int vdev_
 	ret = ath12k_dp_prepare_reo_update_elem(dp, peer, rx_tid);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "failed to alloc update_rxq_list for rx tid %u\n", tid);
-		ath12k_dp_rx_tid_cleanup(ab, &rx_tid->qbuf);
+		/* Nothing has handed the queue to hardware yet.  Undo the
+		 * activation, and free the buffer only if this call allocated
+		 * it.  rx_tid->qbuf is a copy of dp_peer->reoq_bufs[tid], so
+		 * clear that slot too, or the next setup of this TID programs
+		 * the freed buffer into REO.
+		 */
+		peer->rx_tid_active_bitmask &= ~(1 << tid);
+		if (new_qbuf) {
+			ath12k_dp_rx_tid_cleanup(ab, &rx_tid->qbuf);
+			memset(&peer->dp_peer->reoq_bufs[tid], 0,
+			       sizeof(peer->dp_peer->reoq_bufs[tid]));
+		}
 		spin_unlock_bh(&dp->dp_lock);
 		return ret;
 	}
